        "date": "2026-11-07T19:15:05Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(app): judge only axial lathe holes by the axial-hole verdict\n\n`lathe_axial` was true for any lathe Drill, so the axial verdict\n(`drilling::axial_warnings`, which convicts any chain without canned\ncycles) judged every lathe cross drill's radial path and blocked it\n(\"move 1 cuts past the finish surface\"). It now holds only for a lathe\nDrill with no cross holes; the cross arm keeps its own laws (spindle,\nraw-stock standoffs and rapid proof, reach and holder, radial rapids),\nnone of which read `lathe_axial`. Mixed lists stay refused by name.\n\nFixes #80\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
